[h1]GridKitty's Raiding Expanded[/h1]

[b]LAST UPDATED 2026-09-09[/b] - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/changelog/3686119381]READ CHANGELOG FOR DETAILS[/url]

Steal their people. Strip their planets. Fund your own pirate enclave.

[b]Stellaris 4.4.*[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Pop Raiding[/h2]

Raiding forces capture enemy pops through bombardment and invasion. How many you can take is limited, but spending Influence authorizes deeper raids. Each escalation takes more pops, costs more Influence, and draws more galactic attention.

When a tier is filled you choose how to proceed: push deeper, hold position, switch to resource plundering, demand tribute, or force policy changes on the defender. Each choice changes your war goal to match.

You can also authorize [b]Opportunistic Raiding[/b] during any non-raiding war for 50 Influence. You are prompted the first time you try to raid each target, and escalation costs double. Total war authorizes raiding automatically, with no prompt and no cap.

With the caps lifted, raiding can take a colony down to its last pop and destroy it. Any empire you can go to war with is a valid target, fallen empires included.

[h2]Raiding Focus[/h2]

Your raiding focus decides which pops your raiders take and which war goals you can declare. It cannot be changed while at war.

[b]Abduction[/b] takes any eligible pops. [b]Emancipation[/b] targets the enslaved only, and requires slavery to be banned in your own empire. [b]Token Abduction[/b] caps you at 5% of a target's population with no escalation ladder; once you hit the cap your only option is switching to plundering, and finishing a raid grants 12 months of your unity income. [b]Reaping[/b] removes every limit and denies the enemy any chance to surrender.

Reaping is not always available. Xenophobe or Gestalt empires with Barbaric Despoilers, Harvest Incorporated or Nihilistic Acquisition can select it, and Harvesting Protocol and Ravager Swarm get it unconditionally. Declaring a Reaping war carries a severe galaxy-wide opinion penalty that takes decades to decay.

[h2]Plundering[/h2]

Devastation dealt to enemy colonies generates resources based on what those colonies actually produce. Invading a colony cashes out whatever is left. Declaring a [b]Plunder[/b] war increases the yield and guarantees tribute on surrender.

Plunder Yield stacks from base, traditions, civics, and the Plunder war goal. Higher yield means more resources per point of devastation and harsher penalties on the worlds you strip. Occupied planets are raided automatically each month, with captured pops split among allied armies.

[h2]Civics[/h2]

Every empire type gets a pop-raiding civic and a resource-raiding civic.

Pop raiders: [b]Emancipators[/b] and [b]Liberation Enterprise[/b] wage war to free the enslaved. [b]Harvest Incorporated[/b] treats conquered populations as corporate assets. [b]Harvesting Protocol[/b] abducts organics to feed a machine intelligence's power grid, starting with its own battery species.

Resource raiders: [b]Reavers[/b] (Standard) and vanilla [b]Letters of Marque[/b] (Megacorp) strip enemy worlds through the Plundering stance and grant their commanders a plundering trait. [b]Corsair Protocol[/b] (Machine) does the same, grants a ship-breaking trait, and has a 10% chance to capture enemy warships it destroys. The Nomad [b]Void Reavers[/b] civic gains full resource-raiding access.

[b]Ravager Swarm[/b] (Hive) does both. It abducts populations as living biomass for workforce and food, then plunders the ruins for everything else.

[h2]Despoliation Traditions[/h2]

Adopting the Despoliation tree unlocks resource plundering and the Plunder war goal for any empire, plus +1 Plunder Yield if you already had native plundering access. Completing the tree grants an Ascension Perk slot and unlocks the Privateer Enclave.

[h2]Privateer Enclave[/h2]

Found your own pirate haven. It raids on its own, shakes down its victims for tribute, and pays you dividends, while its salvager crews pick through battle wreckage for alloys, minerals, and rare materials.

Upgrade it to expand its fleet, raid more often, and unlock richer payouts. Each enclave gets its own personality when founded. Build a Smuggler's Port on your starbases for extra trade value, and convert between mercenary and privateer enclaves through the diplomacy menu.

[hr][/hr]

[h3]DLC Support[/h3]

Most core features work without DLCs.
They are required for the following:
[list]
[*][b]Overlord[/b]: Privateer Enclave
[*][b]Grand Archive[/b]: Enclave specimens, Boarding Cables tradition variant, and arkship Boarding Cables building (with Nomads)
[*][b]Paragon[/b]: Recovery Fleets council agenda
[/list]

[h3]Compatibility[/h3]

Should be compatible with most mods. Full overwrites:
[list]
[*]Bombardment stance: [i]raiding[/i]
[*]War goals: [i]wg_plunder[/i], [i]wg_plunder_raid[/i]
[*]Casus belli: [i]cb_despoliation[/i], [i]cb_pirate_raid[/i]
[*]Game rules: [i]can_orbital_bombard[/i], [i]should_abduct_pop_group[/i]
[*]Scripted triggers: [i]is_unfriendly[/i], [i]is_slaver[/i], [i]prefers_commander_governors[/i]
[*]Ascension perks: [i]ap_nihilistic_acquisition[/i]
[*]Economic categories: [i]planet_livestock_farmers[/i], [i]planet_livestock_miners[/i], [i]planet_livestock_metallurgists[/i], [i]pop_category_purge[/i], [i]planet_organic_batteries[/i]
[*]Events: [i]enclave.2[/i], [i]enclave.205[/i]
[/list]

